# Disk, floppy and tape images live in diskimages/ and are kept in the
# repository in compressed form only: demo expands "<image>.gz" by itself when
# the image it is told to mount cannot be opened (10.02_devices/2_src/
# storageimage.cpp). The uncompressed copy is a product of a run, and is
# ignored here so it cannot be committed by accident. The ".gz" stays tracked.
#
# Every image carries a ".dsk" extension, the medium in front of it
# (rt11v5.5.rl02.dsk.gz, RTRKV4.00.rk05.dsk.gz), so one pattern covers them all
# - and the pattern cannot collide with the example directories, which are
# named after the medium too (rt11.rl02/, lsx.rx01/). A pattern matches a
# directory as readily as a file, and an excluded directory takes everything
# below it with it.
#
# No image here is anywhere near GitHub's 100 MB limit for a single file; the
# two that are live in the bus-specific trees and are excluded by name in their
# own .gitignore.

*.dsk
